<title>
Rear Lamp House Inner Panel, Rear Lamp House Outer Panel and Side Body Outer Extension (Partial) Removal and Installation
</title>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
The figure below shows condition where the following part are removed.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Back panel: 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A9B06018"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</attention3>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGSB0A9B0132.jpg" width = "183.000mm" height = "74.157mm" ver = "01" gw = "358" gh = "194"/>
</figure>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A9B06022001">
<title>
General Notes
</title>
<ptxt>
Welding method and number of welding points are the same on both sides. This repair instruction shows procedure for right side.
</ptxt>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A9B06022002">
<title>
Removal
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Drill out welding spots and remove rear lamp house outer panel and rear lamp house inner panel.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGSB0A9B0133.jpg" width = "183.000mm" height = "91.065mm" ver = "02" gw = "485" gh = "242"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "4" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "1.968in"/>
<colspec colnum = "3" colname = "3" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "4" colname = "4" colwidth = "1.968in"/>
<tbody>
<row rowsep = "0">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
[A]:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Vehicle inside
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "3" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
[B]:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "4" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Vehicle outside
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</callout>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove side body outer extension (partially) as follows, if necessary.
</ptxt>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Remove quarter-pillar outer panel. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A9B06016"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Mark at the shown position and cut off the side body outer extension.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Drill out welding spot.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGSB0A9B0134.jpg" width = "183.000mm" height = "95.841mm" ver = "01" gw = "280" gh = "255"/>
</figure>
</s2>
</s1>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A9B06022003">
<title>
Installation
</title>
<attention3>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Before conducting any weld, check installation position and condition for installation part(s). 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A9B04005"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Perform repair while taking into consideration installation of parts that affect appearance. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A9B04003"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</attention3>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install new side body outer extension to vehicle body as follows, if removed.
</ptxt>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Install new side body outer extension cut in stacked condition.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Conduct plug weld.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Install quarter-pillar outer panel. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A9B06016"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGSB0A9B0135.jpg" width = "183.000mm" height = "95.841mm" ver = "01" gw = "280" gh = "255"/>
</figure>
</s2>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install rear lamp house outer panel and rear lamp house inner panel.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Conduct resistance spot weld or plug weld.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "ILSB0A9B0031.jpg" width = "183.000mm" height = "91.065mm" ver = "01" gw = "502" gh = "242"/>
